# Ship to main

Production (`app.simy.ch`) deploys only from `main`. `main` is protected.

## Always

1. Branch from `origin/main` (not a dirty feature branch). Keep the hotfix small.
2. Open a PR into `main`. Do not `git push` to `main`.
3. Non-draft PRs to `main` enable squash auto-merge **only when risk is GREEN** (`.github/workflows/auto-merge.yml`). YELLOW, RED, CRITICAL, and unknown never auto-merge. GitHub still merges only when **Test and lint**, **E2E login**, and **Dependency review** are green.
4. Vercel deploys production from `main` after that merge.

## Never

- Treat Cursor / Vercel „6/6“ as enough. That is Bugbot + Vercel previews, not the required Actions jobs. Auto-merge waits only for the required Actions checks, and only for GREEN PRs.
- Use git branch `preview` as a staging path. It is stale and is not production.
- Temporarily drop branch protection to merge, unless the user explicitly asks after Actions failed to start.
- Open a ready PR into `main` unless it should ship. Keep work-in-progress as a **draft**.

## If required checks never appear

Open https://github.com/Kilchi555/driving-team-app/actions. If `CI` did not start within a minute, push a follow-up commit or re-run the workflow. Auto-merge cannot complete while GitHub still says required checks are expected.
